RESOLUTION NO. ________________

ENTITLED:
“A RESOLUTION AMENDING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
AND BOARD OF PUBLIC UTILITIES CONSTRUCTION
SPECIFICATIONS AND STANDARD DRAWINGS, 2007
EDITION.”

WHEREAS, Resolution Numbers 3903, 3970, 4076, 4153, 4321, 4462, 4708, and 4942
address the Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings for work done within
public rights-of-way in the City of Cheyenne and allow for the City Engineer to revise or
amend the Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings in accordance with good
engineering practices; and

WHEREAS, the City Engineer and the Engineering Department of the Board of Public
Utilities have determined that an amendment to the 2007 Edition of the Construction
Specifications and Standard Drawings is necessary; and

WHEREAS, amendments have been prepared by the City of Cheyenne and the Board of
Public Utilities; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne has provided public notice of its intent to adopt the
amended Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings and provided opportunity
for comment regarding the amended Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings.

NOW, THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, THAT the amended City of Cheyenne and
Board of Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall govern
construction of public facilities and construction within public rights-of-way in the City
of Cheyenne.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the amended City of Cheyenne and Board of
Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall be in effect for
all projects and permits approved on or after March 31, 2014.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that a copy of the amended City of Cheyenne and
Board of Public Utilities Construction Specifications and Standard Drawings shall be
kept on file in the Office of the City Clerk, and made available for public inspection at
any time during business hours.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS ______ DAY OF ____________, 2014.

_____________________________________

RICHARD L. KAYSEN, MAYOR

(SEAL)
ATTEST:

___________________________________
CAROL INTLEKOFER, CITY CLERK
```
